# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# YOUR MACHINE, not the tool.
#
# These two files describe one particular setup: absolute paths to your
# ComfyUI, your Blender, your browser profile. They are useless to anyone else
# and they are a map of your machine. The repository ships
# services.example.json and inventory.example.json instead, and the manager
# copies them into place on first run.
#
# Your real files stay exactly where they are on disk — this only stops git
# from tracking them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
services.json
inventory.json

# Agent / editor configuration, not part of the product.
.claude/

# GoReleaser's output, rebuilt by `goreleaser release`.
dist/

# Built binaries — rebuilt with `go build`, never committed.
*.exe
*.exe~

# Runtime state. Everything here is derived and regenerated:
#   cache/       the tool lists, refilled on the first call to each server
#   mcp-manager.log  the tray has no console, so it writes here
cache/
mcp-manager.log

# Timestamped backups the writer leaves NEXT TO the file it touched.
# They usually land in your home directory, but catch any that land here.
*.bak-*

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
